+# PCI DSS Compliance Audit — Payment System
+
+**Task:** 68  
+**Date:** 2026-06-24  
+**Scope:** Schema, Edge Function logging, React Query cache, client persistence  
+**Requirements:** 6, 24 — Acceptance 24A.1, 24A.2, 24A.3
+
+## Executive summary
+
+Renovi does **not** persist raw Primary Account Number (PAN) or Card Verification Value (CVV/CVC) in Postgres, React Query cache, or IndexedDB. Card data transits only over TLS to the NetCred tokenization gateway during the `tokenize-payment-card` Edge Function request lifecycle. Stored references are gateway-issued tokens and masked display values only.
+
+**Result:** PASS — no violations found at audit time.
+
+---
+
+## 1. Schema audit
+
+### 1.1 `payment_tokens` column inventory
+
+| Column | Type | PCI classification |
+|--------|------|--------------------|
+| `id` | uuid | Internal reference |
+| `client_id` | uuid | User reference |
+| `provider_id` | uuid | Gateway reference |
+| `gateway_payment_profile_id` | text | Gateway-issued profile id |
+| `card_number_masked` | text | Masked PAN (display only, e.g. `411111XXXXXX1111`) |
+| `card_brand` | text | Network label (VCC, MASTER, …) |
+| `gateway_card_token` | text | Gateway-issued token reference |
+| `expiry_month` / `expiry_year` | smallint | Expiry metadata (allowed with token reference) |
+| `cardholder_name` | text | Cardholder PII (not PAN/CVV) |
+| `billing_address` | jsonb | Billing PII (not PAN/CVV) |
+| `state` | text | Lifecycle enum |
+
+**Forbidden columns absent:** `pan`, `card_number` (full), `cvv`, `cvc`, `security_code`.
+
+Source migration: `supabase/migrations/20260624000005_create_payment_tokens.sql`
+
+### 1.2 Related payment tables
+
+Automated pgTAP coverage scans all payment-domain tables for forbidden column names:
+
+- `payment_tokens`, `payment_schedules`, `payment_attempts`
+- `payment_webhook_events`, `payment_audit_log`, `payment_events`
+- `payment_webhook_processing_queue`, `payment_providers`, `payment_gateway_tokens`
+- `provider_accounts`, `provider_kyc_submissions`
+
+**Test file:** `supabase/tests/payment/pci_schema_compliance_test.sql`
+
+### 1.3 Verification SQL
+
+```sql
+-- Equivalent manual check
+select c.table_name, c.column_name
+from information_schema.columns c
+where c.table_schema = 'public'
+  and c.table_name like 'payment%'
+  and lower(c.column_name) in ('pan', 'cvv', 'cvc', 'security_code', 'card_number');
+-- Expected: 0 rows
+```
+
+---
+
+## 2. Edge Function log audit
+
+### 2.1 `tokenize-payment-card`
+
+Logger calls in `handleRequest.ts` emit only:
+
+- `payment_provider_not_found` — gateway slug
+- `tokenization_failed` — `client_id`, context, `error_count` (no card payload)
+
+Card fields (`cardData.cardNumber`, `cardData.cvv`) are passed to `deps.tokenizeCard()` and forwarded to NetCred GraphQL; they are **never** passed to `logger.*`.
+
+**Static test:** `supabase/functions/tokenize-payment-card/__tests__/handleRequest_test.ts` — `"handleRequest source does not log raw card fields"`
+
+### 2.2 All payment Edge Functions
+
+Broad static scan of payment EF source files confirms no `logger.*` calls reference `cardNumber`, `cardData`, `cvv`, `securityCode`, or `gateway_card_token`.
+
+**Test file:** `supabase/functions/_shared/payment/__tests__/pci_logging_audit_test.ts`
+
+### 2.3 Gateway adapter
+
+`NetCredAdapter.tokenizeCard` sends PAN/CVV to NetCred over HTTPS only inside the GraphQL mutation body. Span attributes and Sentry payloads exclude card fields (`gateway-spans.ts` records operation/outcome only).
+
+---
+
+## 3. React Query cache audit
+
+Card-touching **mutations** set `gcTime: 0` and `staleTime: 0` so inactive mutation results are discarded immediately:
+
+| Hook | File |
+|------|------|
+| `useTokenizeCard` | `src/features/payments/hooks/useTokenizeCard.ts` |
+| `useAcceptProposalPayment` | `src/features/payments/hooks/useAcceptProposalPayment.ts` |
+| `useInstallmentOptions` | `src/features/payments/hooks/useInstallmentOptions.ts` |
+
+Mutations are **not** dehydrated to IndexedDB by `@tanstack/react-query-persist-client` (queries only).
+
+The saved-cards **query** (`useSavedPaymentTokens`) caches only gateway-safe fields selected in `paymentTokens.api.ts`:
+
+`id, card_number_masked, card_brand, expiry_month, expiry_year, state`
+
+No raw PAN or CVV enters the query cache.
+
+---
+
+## 4. IndexedDB / Capacitor persistence audit
+
+| Storage | Key pattern | Card data? |
+|---------|-------------|------------|
+| IndexedDB (React Query) | `persisted-cache` | Queries only; payment queries contain masked tokens |
+| Capacitor Preferences | `orbit.cache.persist.v1:*` | Auth profile, addresses — no payment card keys |
+| Capacitor Preferences | `orbit_persist_session` | Session preference only |
+| Request quote draft | `orbit.request_quote_draft` | No card fields (checkout is separate flow) |
+
+No payment feature module writes `cardNumber`, `cvv`, or full PAN to `localStorage`, IndexedDB, or Capacitor Preferences.
+
+Card form state lives in React component memory (react-hook-form) and is cleared when the checkout step unmounts after successful tokenization.
+
+---
+
+## 5. Data flow diagram
+
+```
+Browser card form (memory only)
+        │ HTTPS POST { cardData } — transit encrypted
+        ▼
+tokenize-payment-card EF ──► NetCred GraphQL tokenize
+        │                         │
+        │                         └── PAN/CVV stay at gateway
+        ▼
+payment_tokens row: gateway_card_token + card_number_masked
+        │
+        ▼
+Client receives: payment_token_id + masked display fields only
+```
+
+---
+
+## 6. Evidence artifacts
+
+| Artifact | Location |
+|----------|----------|
+| Schema pgTAP | `supabase/tests/payment/pci_schema_compliance_test.sql` |
+| EF logging static test | `supabase/functions/_shared/payment/__tests__/pci_logging_audit_test.ts` |
+| Tokenize EF source audit | `supabase/functions/tokenize-payment-card/__tests__/handleRequest_test.ts` |
+| Table DDL + PCI comment | `supabase/migrations/20260624000005_create_payment_tokens.sql` |
+
+---
+
+## 7. Residual risks & monitoring
+
+1. **Developer regression** — new logger calls or DB columns must be caught by pgTAP + Deno audit tests in CI.
+2. **Sentry breadcrumbs** — payment EFs use structured logging without request body dumps; avoid adding `req.json()` to error context in card flows.
+3. **Third-party gateway** — PCI scope for PAN/CVV storage is delegated to NetCred; Renovi stores tokens only.
+
+**Re-audit trigger:** any schema migration touching `payment_*` tables or changes to `tokenize-payment-card` / checkout hooks.
