+# Orphan PROCESSING Recovery (Operator)
+
+Schedules stuck in `PROCESSING` after an Edge Function crash are recovered automatically by the janitor. Use this runbook when investigating delays or forcing recovery.
+
+## Automatic recovery
+
+| Step | Component | Detail |
+|---|---|---|
+| Lease TTL | `payment_lease_duration_minutes` | 10 minutes |
+| Janitor | `recover-payment-leases` cron | every 30 minutes |
+| Max delay | — | **40 minutes** (see `docs/payment-system/orphan-recovery.md`) |
+
+## Diagnosis
+
+```sql
+select id, contracted_service_id, state, automatic_attempt_count, locked_until, next_retry_at, updated_at
+from public.payment_schedules
+where state = 'PROCESSING'
+order by locked_until nulls last;
+```
+
+Lifecycle context:
+
+```sql
+select public.reconstruct_payment_audit_lifecycle('<contracted_service_id>'::uuid);
+```
+
+## Manual intervention
+
+**Wait** if `locked_until > now()` — the janitor intentionally skips active leases.
+
+If lease expired but janitor has not run:
+
+```sql
+select * from public.recover_orphaned_payment_schedules();
+```
+
+Expected outcomes:
+
+- `automatic_attempt_count = 0` → `SCHEDULED`
+- `automatic_attempt_count > 0` → `FAILED` with `next_retry_at`
+
+## Post-recovery charge behavior
+
+The next cron attempt calls `getTransaction` when `automatic_attempt_count > 1` to reconcile an existing gateway PAID without double-charging (task 65).
+
+## Late commit
+
+Stale EF commits after janitor recovery receive `INVALID_SCHEDULE_STATE` — no state overwrite.
+
+## Related scenarios
+
+- **Stale `REFUND_REQUESTED`:** run `reconcile-netcred-payments` or check gateway refund state.
+- **Sandbox credentials:** halt processing; see `critical-escalation-runbook.md`.
+- **Provider multiple NetCred edges:** verify single `provider_accounts` row per gateway; reconcile onboarding via `detect-netcred-onboarding`.
